@node "About" "About SiL-Comment v1.00"

                               @{"[ MAiN MENU ]"link "MAiN"}
                               @{"[ NEXT PART ]"link "Installation"}

 =========================================================================
                        - About SiL-Comment v1.00 -
 =========================================================================



 I think you know how a comment door works by now so I won't be going
 thrue all that.

 So What's so different about this Comment door compared to others?
 Well for starters, it's a hell of a lot cooler looking.
 Just check out the supplied screenshot! SiL-Comment.iff ...
 It's faster than those slow AREXX scripts (Coded as XiM module using C++).
 It doesn't need any lame configfiles with thousands of control sequences.
 It has a 'Comment-Counter' =)........

 Read the Install for more...

@endnode

@node "Installation" "Installing SiL-Comment v1.00"

                               @{"[ MAiN MENU ]"link "MAiN"}
                               @{"[ NEXT PART ]"link "Package"}

 =========================================================================
                     - Installing SiL-Comment v1.00 -
 =========================================================================


 · Put the Commands/BBSCmd/C.info in it's place.
 · And the Doors/Comment/Comment.xxx
                        /Comment.xxx.info where they belong.

 The datafile that is created by the door and the icons are relative
 to the Comment-door location so you can put them in any drawer you'd like.
@endnode

@node "Config" "Config - SiL-Comment v1.00"

                               @{"[ MAiN MENU ]"link "MAiN"}
                               @{"[ NEXT PART ]"link "Package"}

 =========================================================================
                       - Config SiL-Comment v1.00 -
 =========================================================================


 No stupid configfiles needed just these tooltypes in the Comment.xxx.info

 NAME.1=The Silencer                            <- Name of The SYSOP
 DESC.1=System Operator, Technical Advisor      <- Description

 NAME.2=d-Zire                                  <- Name of CoSysops...
 DESC.2=System Operator, Filenuker, MsgBase     <- Descriptions...

 NAME.3=Rabzi!
 DESC.3=HPA Conferences, Apply 4 Axs Here
 NAME.4=Aquarius
 DESC.4=/X SAS/C Conference Chairman

 Remember the first NAME.1 MUST be the sysop of the BBS.
 -----------------------------------------------------
 Why? Isn't that stupid? No, not at all!
 How many times haven't you logged in to a BBS as a new user being
 prompted to leave a comment? And then when you type C and try to
 choose a sysop it responds:

 Command requires higher access.

 That's because the coder of that Comment door used the 'E' command in /X
 and Not the original 'C' command.
 And ordinarily E is set to a higher security level for validated users
 unlike the C command wich should be accessable by both New users
 as Validated ones.
@endnode

